<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gaius Julius Sohaemus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1st century CE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gaius Julius Sohaemus was the last king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/homs">Emesa</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a>, ruling from 54 CE as a client of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>. He sent troops to support the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> in the Jewish War of 66–73, backed Vespasian's bid for the empire in 69, and took part in the annexation of Commagene in 72. After his reign Emesa was absorbed into the province of Syria.</p></div>
